  "body": "The work of #1649 carries a flipped WCS X or Y, and #760 carries a Z-rotated WCS (Bake and Control). A WCS that is flipped and also rotated is refused by name: \"a flipped and rotated WCS is not supported yet - clear the flip or the rotation\".\n\nThe maintainer's words (2026-11-17), quoted in #1649: \"the ability to flip axis from a positive to negative is fundamental and should not be blocked.. posting and generation should take it into consideration rather..\"\n\nWhat must be decided:\n- The order of the two transforms. A mirror after a rotation by `a` equals a rotation by `-a` after the mirror. The posted G68 angle must have the sign that the controller reads in its mirrored frame.\n- Bake mode: rotate the XY words, then mirror. Control mode: the G68 / ROT angle under a mirror, for each dialect.\n- The travel check and the setup sheet under both.\n\nDone means: a flipped and rotated WCS posts a program that a controller reader traces on the CAM path, in Bake and in Control mode, or a narrower refusal names what is still not carried.\n",
